{%- comment -%}
  The landing page theme's style layer.

  Three sheets, each overriding the one before it. `pluma.css` carries the two
  Hebrew faces and the wrapper. `wf.css` carries the shop: cards, grids, the
  product page. `nv.css` carries the pitch, and it loads last because it
  changes the accent and the grounds for everything above it.

  `pdp.css` and `pl-story.css` are gone. The product page here is `wf-product`,
  which carries its own rules, so neither had anything left to style.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'overflow-list.css' | asset_url | preload_tag: as: 'style' }}
{{ 'base.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}

{%- comment -%}
  Rubik for headlines, Assistant for text. Both are drawn for Hebrew, so the
  page never falls back to a Latin face with patched Hebrew glyphs. Fetched as
  print and promoted on load, so a slow font server cannot hold up first paint.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign pl_fonts = 'https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Assistant:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Rubik:wght@500;600;700&display=swap' -%}
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" as="style" href="{{ pl_fonts }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ pl_fonts }}" media="print" onload="this.media='all'; this.onload=null;">
<noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ pl_fonts }}"></noscript>

{{ 'pluma.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'wf.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'nv.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<script src="{{ 'pluma.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
